# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Daddy's Home" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Talking to Marlo
1	line	Marlo	Hello - it's lovely to see a Mahogany Homes contractor on their rounds! Now, can I help you with something? Or might you be able to do me a little favour?
1	option	What does this Mahogany Homes company do?
2	line	Player	What does this Mahogany Homes company do?
2	line	Marlo	Oh, we redecorate people's houses, fixing things and building new furniture. Mending cabinets, building new chairs and tables - things like that.
2	line	Marlo	When a client hires us to redecorate their house, we send a builder round to do the job, and we ensure the builder's paid for their work.
2	line	Marlo	We can't hire you for that kind of work now, but perhaps you could do me a little favour instead, if you're willing. I can pay!
2	action	other
1	option	What's my current construction contract?
1	option	What kind of favour do you want me to do?
2	line	Player	What kind of favour do you want me to do?
2	line	Marlo	Well, you see, it's about my dad. His house is really decrepit. I need someone to rip out the broken furniture and build him some better stuff. I'll pay you if you do it.
2	option	Aren't you in a construction company yourself though?
3	line	Player	Aren't you in a construction company yourself though?
3	line	Marlo	See, my dad just - um - found the house. No-one was using it, so he just settled in. It's all perfectly harmless, and he's a sick old man anyway, so...
3	line	Marlo	Basically, he's not really meant to be there. And we'd prefer that the landlord not find out, so we're keeping this job off the record. I'll pay you myself.
3	action	other
2	option	Why has he got such a bad house?
3	line	Player	Why has he got such a bad house?
3	line	Marlo	Some kind of economic downturn wiped out his pension plans. It happens more often than you'd think. But I'd rather not talk about it. Can you help him, though?
3	action	other
2	option	Tell me more about the job.
3	line	Player	Tell me more about the job.
3	line	Marlo	Nothing too hard. You'll have to rip out the broken furniture, then build replacements. Dad will talk you through it - he's a retired carpenter himself. He loves talking about construction.
3	option	Aren't you in a construction company yourself though?
4	action	above
3	option	Why has he got such a bad house?
4	action	above
3	option	Tell me where he lives, and I'll do the job.
4	line	Player	Tell me where he lives, and I'll do the job.
4	line	Marlo	Fabulous! Dad lives in the south-east of Varrock, west of Aubury's Rune Shop. His name's Yarlo. Old Man Yarlo, they call him.
4	action	end
3	option	I'd rather not.
4	action	below
2	option	I'd rather not.
3	line	Player	I'd rather not.
3	line	Marlo	Okay, suit yourself.
3	action	end
1	option	Maybe another time.
