1	line	Player	I've been removing the old furniture.
1	line	Old Man Yarlo	You still need to remove: - A broken stool in the kitchen - A broken stool in the bedroom - A broken chair in the bedroom
1	line	Old Man Yarlo	- A broken table in the kitchen - A broken table in the bedroom - The old campbed - The rotten carpet
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Old Man Yarlo again if all the old furniture was removed
1	line	Old Man Yarlo	Ah, young man, how's the redecoration coming on?
1	line	Player	I've finished removing all the old furniture.
1	line	Old Man Yarlo	Jolly good, young man. Now, we'll need to have a talk about what you'll build for me to replace it.
1	line	Old Man Yarlo	You see, I used to be a carpenter myself, before the arthritis got me. Such wonderful things I could build. Let me tell you about the things Construction can do for you...
1	cond	If the player already has a player-owned house:
2	line	Player	Is this necessary? I've got a house of my own, in [city], and I've been learning about Construction for a while.
1	option	Listen to Yarlo.
2	box	As a builder, in your own house, you can create your own rooms full of furniture. A house may start out very basic...
2	box	... but in Building Mode, you'll see what you can add to it...
2	box	... with fancier options available as your Construction level rises.
2	box	You can add lots more rooms, and build their furniture too, unlocking really handy features.
2	box	For example, in a study, you could build a lectern for creating spell tablets, powerful items that can cast spells without runes. You could sell your tablets to other people too.
2	box	A Teleport Nexus can take you to a huge range of destinations, making your home a powerful travel hub.
2	box	Show your dedication to the gods by building an altar, where you can sacrifice bones for bonus Prayer XP.
2	box	With a regeneration pool, you can get healed quickly, before you teleport back to the action.
2	box	The Estate Agents can redecorate your house in different styles, if you want something a bit more impressive.
2	box	And, of course, to make your house feel truly like a home, you can fill it with adorable critters...
2	box	... and drop your guests into the monster pit beneath your throne room.
2	box	All this could be yours, if you train Construction!
2	line	Old Man Yarlo	Now, I was just getting round to telling you about the furniture I want you to build for me. For a start, I'd like two new stools, two new tables and a new chair.
2	box	Some basic wooden planks and some nails should do, for those. I won't ask for anything more fancy - it'd only get stolen anyway, in this neighbourhood.
2	box	I'll want a new carpet too. They can really change the atmosphere of a room, you know! You can buy cloth at the sawmill to make one.
2	line	Old Man Yarlo	Now, for the bed, I've got something special in mind. This town's quite damp, and I don't want the moisture rising up the bed into my blankets. But I've found some wood that resists water.
2	box	Those abandoned crates in the kitchen were here when I moved in, and I found they contain waxwood logs. Waxwood isn't much used in carpentry, but it resists water, so I want a bed made from that.
2	box	You'll have to take three logs from the crate to the sawmill. The chap there will turn them into planks if you mention my name - I've known his family for years.
2	line	Old Man Yarlo	I think that's everything - two stools, two tables, a chair, a bed and a carpet. Off you trot, young man. I'll be here if you have any questions.
2	action	end
1	option	Skip Yarlo's lecture. He'll offer it later if you like.
2	line	Old Man Yarlo	You young people are always rushing around trying to optimise the fun out of life. There are other ways to enjoy the world, you know! But I'm sure you know best.
2	line	Old Man Yarlo	Now, I was just getting round to telling you about the furniture I want you to build for me. For a start, I'd like two new stools, two new tables and a new chair.
2	action	above
